  "body_html": "<h4>Article Index</h4><ul><li><p>When to hold’em and when to fold’em - Managing Fear</p></li><li><p>Broad Stock Market Overview - We Are Trending UP</p></li><li><p>Stocks With Fresh Breakouts - Looking To Buy Something?</p></li></ul><p>One of our positions, Xometry, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$XMTR&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> is up ~25.8% since mid February. One subscriber yesterday had seen my article a bit later, and bought the stock during the overall market drawdown, indicating they bought the dip and they are up 120%. Yes, sometimes some of you all get better prices than me, on my own stock picks 🙄. I honestly just grumble, roll my eyes and chuckle at the same time…but am happy for you all nonetheless lol. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png\" width=\"389\" height=\"173\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:173,&quot;width&quot;:389,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:12703,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/198687498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rnj1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa0883fad-4ff8-49c7-bd86-652ac01db240_389x173.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div></div></div></div><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">120%, no leverage. Never use leverage! Xometry climbed nearly 160% from trough to current price.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The reason I am sharing this, is not to boast…there is enough of that on the internet. The reason is because <em><strong>the journey with Xometry was not smooth</strong></em>…we did experience a period of drawdown, where we had to sit on the stock for a while before getting into a winning position. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png\" width=\"1400\" height=\"768\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:768,&quot;width&quot;:1400,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:202372,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/198687498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!u-0e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff48c6730-d8cd-4ad0-9798-34c38f61a807_1400x768.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">The journey with Xometry has not been smooth. Why did I hold?</figcaption></figure></div><p>The reason I am sharing this story is to answer questions like:</p><ol><li><p>What made me decide to hold through the drawdown?</p></li><li><p>How did I manage the “fear” emotion? And how you can too…</p></li><li><p>When should we actually cut a loss? </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p></li></ol><h4>When To Hold and When To Fold 🃏</h4><p>My long time followers know that I largely operate with 0 indicators. I have some self built tools that tell me trend direction (that is the little triangles on my chart) or breakouts…but you will never catch me with any RSI, MACD or any indicator common amongst retail investors. I started operating with “naked” charts a few years ago, inspired by Tom Hougaard, a massively successful trader and author of “<em><strong><a href=\"https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/best-loser-wins-tom-hougaard/1141387395?ean=9780857198235\">Best Loser Wins</a>”</strong></em>, my 2nd favorite educational trading book I’ve ever read (highly recommend). </p><p>In his book, when Tom was going through his learning stages…struggling…his wife made a simple comment to him during one of his bad trades:</p><p><strong> “What is the stock price doing RIGHT NOW?”</strong></p><p>Price action is KING. </p><p>TREND IS FRIEND. </p><p>Such simple buzz phrases, that often are, erroneously, put in the rear view mirror, in favor of dozens of misleading indicators. </p><p>Recall, we bought Xometry not per the hourly time frame…or the 4 hour time frame…or the daily time frame.<em><strong> Our original time frame was the weekly chart.</strong></em> We bought Xometry, for many reasons, but 1 reason was because the trend was up on the weekly timeframe. </p><p>When we pull up the weekly chart: “What is the stock price doing RIGHT NOW?”</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png\" width=\"1397\" height=\"775\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:775,&quot;width&quot;:1397,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:217244,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/198687498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!vtSt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b1c120f-560f-4dc4-8ec2-b865f5381397_1397x775.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Answer: The stock price is going up. Price action is king. Trend is Friend. </p><p>Yea, the last month of price action sucked. But the only thing we did was carve a higher low. I <strong>decided to hold because trend was intact, per my original investment timeframe</strong> (weekly). </p><p>Do not get shaken out of great positions, by zooming in on smaller timeframes from your original speculation.</p><h4>How to Manage the Fear When Holding</h4><p>Sometimes people have said that I operate like a robot… completely non-emotional to stock price swings. To a degree, they are right. Nearly 20 years of investing and trading, you get numb to volatility over time. But to a degree, they are wrong as well…I am still a human being on the other side of your screen. When a stock (like Xometry) drops shortly after posting, I actually experience more dread than I do fear. Mostly because I know I have to respond to DM’s such as: “What happened to XMTR!?” or “time to cut XMTR?!” (this literally happens every time.) When a stock drops that we bought, I have to begin soothing fear feelings, determining whether its a stock to continue holding and if we do hold, justify why I am holding. Its honestly just a lot of work I often do not want to do lol. Its part of my Substack “job” though, so I accept it…so don’t be shy about asking me ever in the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/b7f4035d-fcb6-44e8-911b-6712dbc96cb7\">Main chat</a>. </p><p>But back to the point: how do I, and you, manage fear? The emotion will never completely go away…but you can train yourself to quell the fear. Largely, I just ask myself “what is the price action doing right now?”…resorting back to that upward arrow above, and walking away. </p><p>Another little personal trick: <strong>turn off chart candles.</strong> I mean it. Turn them off. I cannot tell you how many times a rogue candle wick downwards, on a single day, has scared off investors from a great stock. </p><p>Look at this chart now. What is the AVERAGE price doing? Is the stock making highs? Or making lows? <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/v/D62aWpQ5/\">This tool I built, that you can add to your TradingView chart</a>, plots the 52 period highs and lows (orange lines). We see here that Xometry, on average, is moving upwards (green). There are no new lows, only higher highs. Trend is friend!</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png\" width=\"1406\" height=\"768\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:768,&quot;width&quot;:1406,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:254121,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/198687498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!y_xL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a6fc071-4d4b-4c19-9e27-328964730327_1406x768.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Some people and influencers will conduct analysis paralysis, only for subpar performance, or worse, massive losses. Keep it simple!</figcaption></figure></div><p>Clearly, you can see, there is no point to cut this position. The only thing that is happening is the average price is moving up and new highs are being formed. Odds are good, we would get back into a winning position. </p><h4>When to Cut The Position</h4><p>I wish I could say that I bat 100% accuracy. If you ever find someone that does, let me know, I’ll immediately subscribe to them. Some positions and stocks will go in the gutter. Its inevitable. How you manage those losses, that is what determines the winning investors and losing investors. Recall Tom’s book title: “Best Loser Wins”…title is appropriate.</p><p>Not that accuracy matters much…you could bat maybe 30% accuracy…but if your wins are big enough to offset the losses, is still a winning strategy. Normally, I bounce between 65% to 75% accuracy, and during strong bull trending markets, around 80% accuracy. Yes, I keep logs of all my trades, and all my current positions are tracked live for public view in the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary-fc6?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Summary</a>. </p><p>So when do I accept the loss? Well for a detailed review, I have this article: <em><strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/brief-stock-market-update-when-to?r=4z8lgl\">When to sell</a>. </strong></em>But additionally, I have a “cut price” or “negative % target”. </p><p>Anytime you enter into a position or trade, you MUST have a point on the chart where you say: <strong>“If price reaches $X, I will cut it.”</strong> ALWAYS. I never want to risk more than 2%-3% of my total portfolio equity (personal rule), which you can use the <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/v/G4JKzejz/\">Portfolio Risk Assessment</a> tool to determine your initial position sizing or position % risk tolerance. </p><p>It should be a point, per your initial investment timeframe, you say: <strong>“the trend has changed” or “the trend has stalled.” I</strong>f the position is not making you money, you are wasting your time. Get out. The market works for you, not you work for the market. Period. Yes, you need to let positions “cook” for a period of time. But if its making you take losses, or exposing you to potential large losses…don’t give it your time or money. Walk away. You were wrong. Being wrong will happen sometimes, and that is OK!</p><p>Keep it simple. Ask what the general or average price action is doing. If you answer positively, keep holding. And always have a pre-planned price or percent you say: “this trade is wrong, I am going to cut it so I do not expose myself to a large loss.”</p><h4><strong>What is the Broad Stock Market Up To?</strong></h4><p><strong>Considering the story we talked about above…we are trending upwards. The VIX has been trending down, and the S&amp;P 500 has been making highs. That is all you need to know. Trend is friend. There are numerous stocks climbing rapidly…if you are sitting on the sidelines due to fear from headlines, this is essentially fighting the trend. I understand the sentiment, but the market disagrees with you, and the market is always right.</strong></p><p><strong>If you like this article, please ❤️ and re-stack. It helps massively fight the AI slop here on Substack. </strong></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/cancer-analyzing-test-the-fda-approved?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/cancer-analyzing-test-the-fda-approved?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h4>Now, this stock popped up on the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary-fc6?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screener</a>, breaking out with a 17% gain in a day… trend is friend right?</h4>",
